Subject: [PATCH 4/4] lab(witness): cis_witness verify --strict and panic-free
 receipt parsing (LAB-09 HARDEN-WITNESS)

The tamper sweep of LAB-09 SAFE-01 found that `cis_witness verify` binds the
right fields but reads the receipt leniently: line order, the prompt-toks and
gen-toks values, the header line, unknown lines, duplicate keys, `+25` / `025`
/ upper-case hex and CRLF / trailing blanks were all accepted, and malformed
input made the reader panic instead of failing.

- `verify --strict` (new): accepts only the canonical bytes the writers emit.
  Printable ASCII and LF only; exactly eleven lines in the order of `gen`'s
  println! sequence and aegis-uefi verifier.rs render_receipt (header, model,
  embed, vocab, maxtok, prompt-hex, prompt-toks, gen-toks, token-ids,
  cis-digest, chain), so no unknown, duplicate, missing or reordered line;
  lower-case hex of exact length; canonical decimals (no sign, no leading
  zero); one trailing newline; gen-toks equal to the token-ids count;
  prompt-toks equal to the tokenized prompt length (checked after replay).
  `token-ids ` with an empty value is accepted only for gen-toks 0, which is
  what both writers print. Failures name the line.
- Default `verify` keeps its lenient reader and its output for every input
  that did not panic. Input that used to panic (non-UTF-8 file, unparsable
  maxtok or token id, prompt-hex pair splitting a multi-byte character, empty
  prompt, over-long budget with a checked add instead of a wrapping one,
  multi-byte character in a hash line, missing receipt argument) now ends in
  `VERIFY FAIL - <reason>` and exit 1; unreadable or unusable files exit 2.
- `gen` prints through render_receipt(); its output is byte-identical to the
  previous binary (checked on 7 prompts including max_new 0).
- Cargo.toml: test = true for the cis_witness example, so its 9 unit tests
  (golden fixtures, writer/reader key order, every leniency class, truncation
  at every byte) run under `cargo test`.

Validation (Ranger3143 labs/logs/safe/HARDEN-WITNESS/RESULT.md): the 6381
SAFE-01 mutant rows re-run through both modes: 0 panics in either mode (the
previous binary crashed on 222); default verdicts unchanged except those 222
crash-rejects, now clean rejections; of the 838 mutants in C08 and U1-U6 that
the previous default accepted, --strict accepts 0; the 11 QEMU-minted
receipts, the m7 golden fixture (replayed with its artifacts) and 164 gen-minted
receipts pass under --strict; 2400 seeded malformed inputs: 0 panics in both
modes. aegis-core tests unchanged (159 passed). No performance claims (Rule A).

